---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import proof from '../lib/readiness.json';
---
<Base title="Get Ready, before an idea" description="Let your coding agent verify the actual workspace, GitHub, Cloudflare, DNS and tools, then prove a real HTTPS deployment before you choose an app."><h1>Get Ready.</h1><p class="lede">Your agent runs the checks and deploys a small reference. You only handle authentication or approval that needs a person.</p><div class="workbench"><section><h2>Start with your agent.</h2><p>Open your project in Codex and copy the setup handoff. Your agent checks the tools, accounts and domain, then proves a deployment.</p><button class="button" id="copy-ready">Copy to Codex</button><p id="message" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="message"></p><details><summary>Read the agent handoff</summary><pre id="ready-prompt">Prepare my development environment before asking what I want to build. Use App Composer’s current Get Ready implementation: https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer. Read trusted AGENTS.md. Run the repository-owned readiness doctor against the actual workspace. Select the authorised Cloudflare account, Hello Worker name, HTTPS origin and exact GitHub reference repository; never reuse the launch operator’s account or domain for another person. Preserve the private action-required receipt and resume after human authentication; verify Git, GitHub CLI authentication and repository access, the coding-agent runtime, Cloudflare/Wrangler and intended domain/DNS. Use an existing authorised account. If the reviewed Hello checkout is missing project dependencies, use the supported install-reference-tools operation and verify the local tools before deployment. Global tools use their official supported installers. Deploy the configurable Hello World reference, verify exact build identity over HTTPS, change one value and verify the redeployment. Save private resumable evidence, never credentials. Ask MP only for unavoidable authentication, purchase, expanded permission or consequential approval. Continue independent checks if one step is blocked. Report the exact human action, if any. Do not invent an idea or claim readiness from a checklist.</pre></details><details><summary>Already prepared?</summary><p>Run <code>pnpm ready</code> in the actual Composer checkout. A fork or another workspace supplies <code>--workspace</code>, <code>--account</code>, <code>--reference-worker</code>, <code>--reference-url</code> and <code>--reference-repo</code>. The doctor checks account routing as well as HTTPS source identity. It saves failed checks, continues independent checks and resumes after authentication. Provider interruptions stay with the agent for retry; they do not automatically require another human sign-in. The receipt expires and records tool versions, source identity and the selected HTTPS proof. Changes to account, repo, domain or tools require the relevant check again. Private receipts stay on your device.</p><p>The same core can run independently through the <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/blob/main/examples/get-ready.mjs">standalone Node example</a>. Its optional setup operation installs missing pinned dependencies in a reviewed Hello checkout on the supported Mac toolchain, then resumes the same checks. Reference deployment is limited to the reviewed Hello source and an existing authorised account, Worker and route. <a href="/docs#standalone-get-ready">See the supported boundary.</a></p></details><a href="/init">Explore the Init form</a></section><aside class="ink"><h2>This operator’s verified path</h2><p class="note">This evidence belongs to the App Composer launch environment. It does not make a visitor’s environment ready.</p>{proof.checks.map(c=><div class="status"><strong>{c.label}</strong><span>{c.status}</span><p class="note">{c.detail}</p></div>)}<div class="actions"><a class="button" href={proof.url}>Open the HTTPS reference</a></div><p class="note">{proof.reviewed} · <a href="/release">Source and release proof</a></p></aside></div><section class="section split"><div><h2>You don’t need a project yet.</h2><p>The Hello World reference can be retained and customised, or left behind when your real app is ready. A temporary Cloudflare address avoids a domain purchase. Existing custom domains are checked for conflicts before routing changes.</p></div><div><h3>What the agent verifies</h3><ul><li>The actual repo, clone and GitHub permissions.</li><li>The available coding-agent and deployment tools.</li><li>The selected account, domain and DNS route.</li><li>The exact deployed identity over HTTPS.</li></ul><p>Models, registrars and browser plugins beyond this supported path remain separate integrations, never assumed from a logo.</p></div></section><script>document.querySelector('#copy-ready')!.addEventListener('click',async()=>{try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.querySelector('#ready-prompt')!.textContent!);document.querySelector('#message')!.textContent='Copied. Your agent now owns the preparation work.';}catch{document.querySelector('#message')!.textContent='Clipboard access failed. Select and copy the handoff above.';}});</script></Base>
